<description>&lt;p&gt;Venezuelan authorities detained former world champion boxer Linares while appointing a gay foreign minister, reflecting internal political shifts, and workers staged a 24‑hour strike at Miraflores Palace as the government allocated US$12 billion of oil revenue to support the bolívar. A special-forces soldier who wagered $400,000 on Maduro's removal appeared in court, and a marine died after falling overboard during the first US military operation in the Caribbean. Trump announced Venezuela as a new acquisition and claimed superior armaments, while a Venezuelan military attaché resumed work in Minsk and EU asset freezes targeted Haitian gangs linked to the crisis. Two battle-related deaths occurred in 2007, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Al Jazeera&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMivAFBVV95cUxNNXIyMjB0bmNDczNUZ2dldlNWWmJuZlFBX0lhZmJWVThuWVFIVlIzN2dDSXU2ai1QVTFjemxKQ2hENkUxZEFtekl6WktjazBKSkhocWZJRm5fXzZ6MFFGU052ZVpaWWNiaHNudkpRMTM1MUF6akdZOXp3azg0RkNxaUY2VUZTSV9JbWlUU2hGOF91WkcxQXV2NmRGZGpDbHZEbG9YejMwZjV6dkZ3Mm5LRHMwaDdnZzVLS2R5bw?oc=5&quot;&gt;France 24&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiYkFVX3lxTE50eDNKRkY5SFZtOS1CRE1XRDEzbEwteXVicVhGXzF2V0R6MDRCWlVNcE94SE9UTjUyWl85NDZ5a3c1ZjZZcDh0NkJoNzFLRXkzM0dTc1pIM1Zvc2NtdVgwVkpn?oc=5&quot;&gt;Foreign Policy in Focus&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMikwFBVV95cUxNR0xHQkhLbXVzN203ZW82SHltSGhvM05LTk5IZlRrcDRab3JWNEJvNkJJYnZiU2xkUEdHNjZXbXE5Y3MwR0U0d2k5djZsa0lmNGpQMGVsUXlwc3FWakJ5MWY3NDZrSTk0amp2WnZROG5qdVVGQlhUR01Fbzhlb2d3emRhT3ptVHlIdFJXY2ZWeDRpQXM?oc=5&quot;&gt;Caracas Chronicles&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiekFVX3lxTE5wLUJ5MVh3d3FDSEhnWndEZm5QWlJ1TkFNbEhuMHFoUTJzZFBKQ1Z0NjExVmtXX3dNc0JB